NeuroWard — Single-File HTML Neurology Ward App

Stack: Vanilla JS, localStorage + IndexedDB shadow backup, no framework, no server. Runs in browser. One file, self-contained.

Data model (global arrays):

	•	patients[] — active ward patients, key STORAGE_KEY
	•	archived[] — discharged/removed, key ARCHIVE_KEY
	•	trash[] — from archive, key ARCHIVE_KEY+'_trash'
	•	currentId — currently selected patient ID
	•	Each patient has _updatedAt ISO timestamp, set by upd() on every edit

Core data functions:

	•	saveD() → localStorage + IDB write + debounced cloud push (2s)
	•	saveArchive() / saveTrash() → localStorage + IDB write
	•	upd(fn) → patches current patient, stamps _updatedAt, calls saveD()
	•	loadD() → loads all three arrays from localStorage
	•	migrate() → adds missing fields to old patient records (always run after load)
	•	getP() → returns current patient object

Patient object structure (key fields):

id, name, nameAr, age, sex, doa, dos, diagnosis, ddx, referringStaff,
occupation, marital, residence, handedness, templateKey,
complaint, hpi, pastHistory, personalHistory, familyHistory,
exam: {general, cn, tone, RUL, LUL, RLL, LLL, reflexesSup, reflexesDeep,
       plantar, sensSup, sensDeep, coordination, gait, cognition},
specificLabs[], otherLabs[], imaging[], npStudies[], ophthalInv[], cultures[],
routineLabs[],   ← [{date, values:{Hb,WBC,PLT,INR,PTT,Fibrinogen,Na,K,
                      Creatinine,Urea,ALT,AST,Albumin,CRP,Ca,Mg,Bilirubin,ALP}}]
abg[],           ← [{date, values:{pH,PaO2,PaCO2,HCO3,BE,SaO2,FiO2,PF}}]
vitals[],        ← [{date, temp,hr,bp,rr,o2,wt, ventMode,fio2,peep,tv,rrSet,ie,pip,pplat,ps}]
consultations[], treatments[], antibiotics[], concurrentMeds[],
devices[], hospitalCourse[], scales[], problemList[], tasks[],
attachments[], collapsedSections{}, dischargeMeds, dischargeInstructions,
_updatedAt, _archivedDate, _deleted

Investigation items (specificLabs, imaging, etc.): {id, name, status, orderedDate, doneDate, result}Status cycle: not-ordered → ordered → pending → done-pending-result → resulted

Treatment objects:

	•	IVMP: {type:'IVMP', startDate, daysTotal}
	•	IVIG: {type:'IVIG', startDate, daysTotal, dose}
	•	PLEX: {type:'PLEX', startDate, sessionsTotal, frequency, labsDone, mahurkarDone, mahurkarDate, mahurkarSide, mahurkarSite}
	•	Antibiotics: {drug, startDate, stopDate, days, indication, status:'active'|'stopped', abType}
	•	ConcurrentMeds: {name, dose, startDate, stopDate, status:'active'|'onhold'|'stopped'}
	•	Devices: {type, insertionDate, removalDate, site, condition}
	•	Scales: {id, scaleId, entries:[{date, value, notes}]}

UI structure:

	•	Fixed top bar (#fab-wrap): day badge, 📱 mobile toggle, ☁ cloud button, ⚕ FAB menu
	•	#sidebar (240px): patient list with alert dots, search, Admit/Template buttons, Archive button
	•	#main: patient header (#pthdr) with alert badges + action buttons, then collapsible sec sections
	•	Mobile mode (body.mobile-ui): layout stacks vertically, fab-wrap becomes fixed full-width top bar, layout gets padding-top:46px

Section keys (used in collapsedSections and DOM IDs s-{key}, sb-{key}, sh-{key}):
problems, history, exam, investigations, labs, vitals, consults, treatment, scales, devices, course

Render flow: selPt(id) → renderPt() → builds all sections as innerHTML → wires del-pt-btn via addEventListener. Section toggle: togSec(key). Alert badges call jumpTo('s-{key}').

Alerts system (getAlerts(p)):
Returns [{lv:'r'|'y'|'b'|'t', msg, anc:sectionKey}]Red (r): abnormal labs (! suffix), expired antibiotics, PLEX prereqs missing, abnormal vitalsYellow (y): ordered/pending investigations, awaiting consults, stopped medsBlue (b): active treatment day counters

Lab abnormal flag: append ! to any value (e.g. 7.2!) → turns red, fires alert until a later entry has a normal value for the same key.

8 Clinical templates (in TEMPLATES object):
ms, mg, nmo, enceph, gbs, stroke, ich, sah, infection, epilepsyEach pre-orders investigations, treatments, consults, and populates histGuide/examGuide arrays shown as collapsible boxes in History and Exam sections.

Clinical scales library (SCALE_LIB): GCS, NIHSS, mRS, Barthel, MoCA, MMSE, ASPECTS, ABCD², ICH Score, Hunt & Hess, Fisher, WFNS, Graeb, EDSS, SDMT, MG-ADL, QMG, GBS Disability, MRC Sum, EGRIS, STESS, CASE, Hoehn & Yahr, UPDRSSuggested per diagnosis via suggestScales(diagnosis).

DOCX exports (all use docx@8.5.0 CDN via ensureDocx(cb)):

	1.	Med-Fil-48 (buildMedFil48Docx) — compact A4 card, lab trend table (admission/72h/discharge), vitals, course, meds
	2.	Full Discharge (buildFullDischargeDocx) — comprehensive multi-section document, lab table per date, ABG table, investigations split into resulted vs ordered/pending, vitals table, all sections
	3.	Ward 15 (buildWard15Docx) — official 2-page department form with embedded base64 header image, Times New Roman, grey-shaded label cells, exam on/off discharge columns, discharge meds numbered in Arabic numerals

Cloud sync (Supabase):

	•	Creds stored in localStorage: SB_URL_KEY, SB_KEY_KEY
	•	Table schema: neuroward_patients(id text PK, data jsonb, updated_at timestamptz)
	•	sbPushAll() — upserts all patients with their _updatedAt as updated_at
	•	sbPull(silent) — incremental: uses ?updated_at=gt._lastPullTime filter; compares remoteTime !== localTime; calls renderPt() if open patient updated
	•	startPolling() — 45s setInterval, skips when tab hidden, shows toast on update
	•	_lastPullTime — tracks last pull; set to null for full re-fetch (manual pull / new connect)
	•	setSyncStatus(state, msg) — updates dot + label in top bar. States: local|syncing|synced|error
	•	sbDelete(ptId) — soft-delete: pushes {_deleted:true} then removes locally

IDB shadow backup:

	•	openIDB(), idbWrite(patients) — writes {date, patients, archived, trash} to IndexedDB
	•	On startup: if localStorage empty but IDB has data → shows restore banner
	•	saveArchive() and saveTrash() also trigger idbWrite()

BroadcastChannel: syncs between tabs in same browser, also refreshes archive count.

AI features:

	•	Scan (openScan(), runScan()) — photos → Claude API → extracts structured data → applyScan() saves to patient
	•	AI Summary (genAISummary()) — sends full patient data → structured handover summary
	•	Both use apiHeaders() which injects stored API key if outside claude.ai

Key helper functions:

	•	fmtD(d) → “28 Nov” format
	•	td() → today as YYYY-MM-DD
	•	esc(s) → HTML escape
	•	isAbn(v) → ends with !
	•	stripB(v) → removes trailing !
	•	admDay(doa) → “Day N”
	•	dSince(d) → days since date
	•	uid() → random 7-char ID
	•	mkInv(name) → new investigation object
	•	mkSpark(vals) → inline SVG sparkline

